{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>There shall not be to you.</b> Why is this said? Since it is said ״לֹא תַעֲשֶׂה לְךָ״ — that tells me only that he may not make them; from where do I know that he may not keep one already made? Scripture says: ״לֹא יִהְיֶה לְךָ״ (ibid.)." "<b>Other gods.</b> They are not divinities at all — others made them into gods for themselves. And it is not fitting to explain it as 'gods other than Him,' for it would be a disparagement toward above to call them divinities alongside Him. Another interpretation: 'other gods' — they are 'others' to their worshipers: they cry out to them and they do not answer them, and it is as though he is a stranger whom he has never known." "<b>Before My face.</b> All the while that I exist — so that you do not say: we were not commanded concerning idolatry except for that generation (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:15.560584731Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}